To fix this, you need to grab the postingDate from your React state, format it back to the standard backend format (YYYY-MM-DD), and inject it into every row payload before submitting.
Right now, your rowPayloads.push() does not include any date field, which is why your backend is falling back to the current system date.
Here are the exactly lines you need to update inside your **handleSubmit** function.
### 1. Format the Date for the Backend
Your frontend stores postingDate as DD-MM-YYYY (e.g., 28-02-2026) for display purposes. Spring Boot expects YYYY-MM-DD.
Add this conversion right after you set setIsSubmitting(true) at the top of handleSubmit:
```javascript
    setIsSubmitting(true);

    // Convert DD-MM-YYYY back to YYYY-MM-DD for Spring Boot
    const [day, month, year] = postingDate.split("-");
    const formattedBackendDate = `${year}-${month}-${day}`;

    const cglCheck = new Map();
    // ... rest of your existing code

```
### 2. Inject the Date into the Payload
Scroll down in handleSubmit to where you are building the rowPayloads array. Add the new date field to the object.
*(Note: Ensure the key name postingDate exactly matches the new variable name you set in your backend Java DTO. If you named it pDate in Java, use pDate here).*
```javascript
      const finalAmount =
        row.txnType === "Credit" ? "-" + row.amount : row.amount;

      rowPayloads.push({
        branch: row.branch.code,
        currency: row.currency,
        cgl: row.cgl.cglNumber,
        amount: finalAmount,
        productType: row.productCode,
        remarks: row.remarks,
        arFlag: "A",
        postingDate: formattedBackendDate // <--- ADD THIS LINE
      });
    }

```
### Why this works:
Because you successfully fetched the official posting date from /JS/journals/current-posting-date on page load, it is locked into your postingDate state. By adding postingDate: formattedBackendDate to the payload, you are explicitly forcing the backend to use that official date instead of LocalDate.now() for every single row in the batch.
